/**
 * @page data_structures_reference Data Structures Reference
 * @brief How to read the generated data-structure index.
 * @ingroup module_data_structures
 *
 * The complete alphabetical index is generated from the declarations in the
 * source tree.  Each structure's description belongs next to its definition,
 * where its fields, ownership, lifetime, and synchronization rules are
 * visible.  The index therefore stays useful as the implementation changes
 * instead of accumulating a second, stale description of every type.
 *
 * For the main design overviews, see the topics for networking, media, audio,
 * sessions, UI, and tooling.  Use the generated structure pages for field
 * details and the owning subsystem's topic for lifecycle rules.
 */
